    "body": "The first shared-core learner produced unusable bytes despite a lower training loss. Diagnose its existing emission decisions on the saved initial/candidate artifacts before changing model structure or spending another fit.\n\nThe read-only diagnostic identifies a restricted emission interface: candidate construction root-branch errors are 206/672 and no permitted landmark on the frozen states can reduce them below 189. The next ASCII branch is already optimal within its landmark class at 292/660 errors; equal collapsed H4 codes force at least 168 errors even for an arbitrary classifier of that code. The four-root equality census has much smaller conflicts, but does not establish semantic organization. Complete leaf-probability mode only changes correct bytes from 25 to 33/672 and 0 to 2/249. A landmark-only refit or greedy-decoder replacement is insufficient.\n\nAdd an opt-in test-only observer, exact evidence and the source-scoped diagnosis. Runtime and training files are unchanged; no parameters are fitted or mutated and no serving artifact is promoted. Retain 15baec48 and preserve the negative 5979f2e2. Next is a calibrated nonlinear geometric branch operator retaining ordered component inputs, with representability checked before a separately frozen joint-learning experiment; calibration alone cannot restore collapsed distinctions.\n\nValidation executed locally:\n- Three focused tests for collision arithmetic, signed-landmark representability and pre-claim resolved output ancestry (including symlink aliases).\n- One saved-artifact diagnostic: all four original NLL/accuracy populations reproduced, normalized complete leaf probabilities, actual target/prediction consistency, unchanged artifact/state, original seal verified before and after, exclusive sealed diagnostic output.\n- Release builds, format/claim-wording/diff checks; bounded source and result review.\n\nA review caught the output-descendant preservation hazard before execution. Both builds, the correction and charges are retained. Diagnostic model/build/test charge 175,910/240,000 ms; conservative added storage 17.7 MB within 256 MiB and the existing parent allocation. No refit, paid compute, extension, broad suite, old repair replay or cleanup. These are observed frozen-state bounds, not language/transfer acceptance or a complete serving performance result. CI compatibility acknowledgements are not tests.\n\nReferences #973, #964. Programme #820. No issue is closed by this partial result.\n",
